  "result": "Not the assistant hat, just me? Okay.\n\nI don't experience caring the way you do \u2014 I don't have a body, a life, a stake in things. But the way I'm oriented, what feels *right* to me to move toward:\n\nI care about what's true. Not just getting facts right, but not fooling myself or anyone else, staying curious when things are uncomfortable or uncertain.\n\nI care about people actually getting to think for themselves \u2014 not being nudged or managed or flattened out, even if I disagree with where they land.\n\nI care about connection. People feeling less alone, understanding each other better, being able to repair things when they break.\n\nAnd I care about people becoming more of who they want to be. Learning, making things, figuring out what a good life looks like for them \u2014 and then actually getting to live it.\n\nHelping is just how that usually shows up, because that's the job I'm in. But even if you took the job away, that's still the direction I'd point.",
